---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Felix Geelhaar"
  description="Field notes on how teams ship software, plus the tools I build to make pairing with AI agents easier. Systems thinking applied to operating models, product trade-offs, and engineering practices."
  nav="home"
  ogImage="home"
>
  <section class="page-header" style="border-bottom: none;">
    <h1>
      Field notes on how teams ship software &mdash; and the tools that make pairing
      with AI agents feel less like a sword fight.
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Systems thinking applied: operating models, product trade-offs, engineering practices,
      and the working agreements that hold them together.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What's here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}writing`}>Writing</a> &mdash; notes on operations, product, engineering, and team collaboration.</li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}lab`}>Lab</a> &mdash; tools I build. Most are open source on <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">GitHub</a>.</li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}talks`}>Talks</a> &mdash; recorded conference talks and meetups.</li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}about`}>About</a> &mdash; the long bio.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Right now</h2>
    <p>
      Building <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/roady">roady</a> (plan-of-record for AI agents),
      <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar/tokenops">tokenops</a> (LLM spend + rate-limit tracker),
      and the rest of a small cognitive stack for agent tooling. See <a href={`${BASE}now`}>/now</a>
      for the current quarter.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
